You can run Podman directly from Git Bash on Windows.
1. Verify Podman installation
podman --version


2. Initialize Podman machine
podman machine init --provider wsl


If the machine is already initialized, skip this step.
3. Start Podman
podman machine start


Verify:
podman machine list
podman info


4. Create and run a container
For an Ubuntu container:
podman run -dit \
  --name ubuntu-test \
  docker.io/library/ubuntu:24.04 \
  bash


Enter the container:
winpty podman exec -it ubuntu-test bash


winpty helps Git Bash handle interactive terminals on Windows.

For an NGINX container:
podman run -d \
  --name nginx-test \
  -p 8080:80 \
  docker.io/library/nginx:latest


Test:
curl http://localhost:8080


5. Manage containers
podman ps -a
podman start ubuntu-test
podman stop ubuntu-test
podman rm -f ubuntu-test

